# vdbvisualizeslice

- Label: VDB Visualize Slice
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 1 to 1
- Parameters: 11 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/vdbvisualizeslice.html
- Summary (EN): Extracts a slice from a VDB and outputs it as mesh geometry so the voxels can be viewed directly. It matches the Volume Slice SOP but runs inside COPs. Output: slice (geometry with the extracted points).
- Résumé (FR) : Extrait une coupe d'un VDB et la sort en géométrie pour voir les voxels directement, sans changer de contexte.

- Inputs meaning: ["vdb: a Float, Vector or Integer VDB to visualize; Integer VDBs are first converted to colour through the ID to RGB COP"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: the VDB type the source accepts", "Plane: the volume-local axis to slice along", "Relative Location: place the plane relative to the volume, or in world coordinates", "Position: starting point for the slice in world coordinate mode", "Offset: relative mode, -1 to 1 spans the full range (0 is the centre); world mode shifts along the world axis perpendicular to the plane", "Snap to Voxel: slice values come from original voxels rather than blends of two neighbours", "Visualization Min / Max: VDB values mapped to the start and end of the colour ramp", "Visualization Ramp: colour scheme; with multiple volumes the first three map to red, green and blue"]

- Caveats: ["Without Snap to Voxel, slice values may be blends of two voxels when the offset does not fall exactly on a voxel", "In world coordinate mode on a rotated volume, the offset does not align with the volume axes"]

